WEBVTT

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.950
All right, everyone! Get to work!

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.580
Yeah!

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.270
Your magic is so useful, Well.

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.340
You flattened everything in an instant.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:28.310
Man, I can't believe the count's magic 
is actually being used for development.

00:01:31.680 --> 00:01:34.330
I'll be heading back now, Roderich.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:37.020
One moment, milord.

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:39.050
Can you take care of that area next?

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:03.610
I'm back.

00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:06.060
Welcome home!

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:09.650
Welcome home.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.770
Thanks, Elise.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:18.690
Hup.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.790
Here you go.

00:02:22.790 --> 00:02:23.620
Thank you.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.520
You seem tired.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:31.270
Yeah. He ran me into the ground again today.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.170
Your relationship with him is really topsy-turvy.

00:02:36.730 --> 00:02:39.940
It's like Roderich's your boss.

00:02:40.570 --> 00:02:43.410
Like you're his slave, Lord Well.

00:02:43.760 --> 00:02:46.360
To be fair, no matter how far I go,

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:48.510
I'm a white-collar office worker at heart.

00:02:50.820 --> 00:02:52.200
"White-collar"?

00:02:55.590 --> 00:02:57.580
Anyway, I'm gonna go get changed.

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:14.780
It's not so easy to change, huh?

00:03:16.180 --> 00:03:18.480
Even though it was ten years ago...

00:03:19.530 --> 00:03:21.350
that I was an office worker.

00:03:25.390 --> 00:03:26.770
I'm home.

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.300
No! Gotta wake up!

00:03:50.230 --> 00:03:52.530
<i>Quick Cooking Mode activated.</i>

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:57.460
White Rice          Brown Rice

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:57.460
Quick Cooking

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:57.460
24 Minutes Left

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.700
<i>Rice will be ready in 24 minutes.</i>

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:25.960
A midnight one-soup, three-dish dinner: 
miso-fried pork ribs version.

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:29.610
Now just add the radish sprouts...

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.580
White Rice          Brown Rice

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.580
Quick Cooking

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.580
2 Minutes Left

00:04:57.450 --> 00:05:00.260
<i>Huh? Where are the pork ribs?</i>

00:05:29.850 --> 00:05:32.110
Wait, am I overseas?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.190
Now that I've finally seen my successor wed,

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:40.690
I can retire without worry.

00:05:37.600 --> 00:05:39.120
<i>But they're speaking Japanese.</i>

00:05:40.690 --> 00:05:43.160
Father, please stop joking.

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:52.500
Boy, this is one realistic dream.

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:54.950
Okay.

00:05:55.910 --> 00:05:57.800
time to go back to my pork ribs.

00:06:02.800 --> 00:06:05.260
What do you think you're doing?

00:06:05.690 --> 00:06:06.790
Wake up!

00:06:09.760 --> 00:06:12.730
Come, you must greet everyone.

00:06:14.570 --> 00:06:15.690
But my pork ribs...

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:18.090
Sorry to have kept you waiting.

00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:20.010
This is my youngest son.

00:06:22.100 --> 00:06:24.440
Is <i>this</i> real life?

00:06:24.440 --> 00:06:26.170
What are you saying?

00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:29.900
Now, introduce yourself. You can do that, yes?

00:06:30.690 --> 00:06:33.870
Intro... Introduce myself?!

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.800
U-Uh...

00:06:42.130 --> 00:06:43.340
Er...

00:06:44.650 --> 00:06:45.660
What's wrong?

00:06:48.380 --> 00:06:50.470
It's good to finally see you all again.

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:53.880
Oh, Erich?

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:55.590
How you've grown.

00:06:55.590 --> 00:06:59.770
We're very grateful that you took 
the time to come all the way

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:01.600
for my eldest brother Kurt's wedding.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:07.670
Allow my younger brother, 
Wendelin von Benno Baumeister,

00:07:07.670 --> 00:07:10.170
and I to express our most profound thanks.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:13.850
Was that my name?

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:15.560
Wendelin?

00:07:15.560 --> 00:07:18.030
Can I call you Well, then?

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:22.320
Well? Y-Yes, of course.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.210
Here.

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:27.820
Thanks.

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:31.200
Did your mind go blank when you
 found yourself surrounded by adults?

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:35.080
Uh, what's happening today?

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:38.440
Ah, I suppose it's a little 
complicated for a five-year-old.

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.920
Today is Brother Kurt's wedding.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:46.760
The bride is Amalie, the second 
daughter of Sir Mainbach.

00:07:47.620 --> 00:07:50.480
Father was having trouble
 finding a partner for him.

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:55.570
He must be relieved that a noble's 
daughter has married into the family.

00:07:55.980 --> 00:07:57.570
A noble?

00:08:02.560 --> 00:08:06.390
Hey, if a noble's daughter 
is marrying into our family,

00:08:06.390 --> 00:08:09.840
are we by any chance nobles, too?

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:14.310
"By any chance"? I suppose 
I can see why you'd be doubtful.

00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:18.560
But we Baumeisters are genuine nobility, too.

00:08:22.270 --> 00:08:23.850
Nobility...

00:08:26.720 --> 00:08:27.830
One more time!

00:08:28.970 --> 00:08:32.250
<i>Who could ever see this coming?</i>

00:08:39.280 --> 00:08:43.250
From Duke Bleichröder

00:08:40.150 --> 00:08:43.250
<i>But I can understand the language, at least.</i>

00:08:44.060 --> 00:08:47.220
<i>If we can throw such a lavish ceremony,</i>

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:49.890
<i>we must rank pretty high up.</i>

00:08:52.080 --> 00:08:54.130
<i>And if I'm the third son of this family,</i>

00:08:55.020 --> 00:08:58.230
<i>I don't have to worry about starving!</i>

00:09:07.910 --> 00:09:10.510
Noble food is so yummy!

00:09:41.680 --> 00:09:43.510
This is so dry...

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:51.820
And this soup is basically just water.

00:10:07.950 --> 00:10:09.990
What's wrong, Wendelin?

00:10:09.990 --> 00:10:11.110
Nothing.

00:10:12.860 --> 00:10:15.190
You can't have more soup, okay?

00:10:15.730 --> 00:10:18.830
Um, where's Brother Erich?

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.450
He left earlier, saying he was going fishing.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:24.920
"We must rank pretty high up"?

00:10:25.910 --> 00:10:27.670
Was that some kind of joke?

00:10:27.670 --> 00:10:31.510
But we threw such a glittering 
party last night.

00:10:31.510 --> 00:10:32.780
Well, yeah.

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:38.950
We can't be cheapskates with invited guests,
 even as poor as we are.

00:10:38.950 --> 00:10:39.990
Poor?

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:42.730
You could say it was a show of noble pride.

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:58.950
Th-Then what about the noble fo—I mean, dinner?

00:10:59.350 --> 00:11:03.270
A special menu for the wedding, of course.

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:06.910
But we're back to brown bread 
and light soup starting today.

00:11:06.910 --> 00:11:08.060
No way...

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:11.830
<i>But even if we're poor, we're still nobility.</i>

00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:14.500
<i>There's Brother Kurt, Brother Erich...</i>

00:11:14.500 --> 00:11:18.710
<i>And I'm the third son, 
so I should get some benefits, at least.</i>

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:21.360
Oh, how did the hunt go, Brother Helmut?

00:11:21.840 --> 00:11:23.020
No good.

00:11:23.020 --> 00:11:24.970
I couldn't catch a thing.

00:11:26.340 --> 00:11:28.360
<i>Brother Helmut?</i>

00:11:28.360 --> 00:11:30.280
<i>Then I'm the...</i>

00:11:30.280 --> 00:11:33.460
Horohoro really are hard to shoot down.

00:11:33.460 --> 00:11:35.740
Even for you, Brother Paul?

00:11:35.740 --> 00:11:37.700
<i>Brother Paul?</i>

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:41.790
The horohoro served at the wedding was so good.

00:11:41.790 --> 00:11:45.670
Yeah, I saw you eating 
one whole, Brother Hermann.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:47.720
<i>Brother Hermann?!</i>

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:52.910
Speaking of the wedding, 
Walter and Karl didn't show up.

00:11:52.910 --> 00:11:55.600
It's understandable. 
Even if they are our brothers...

00:11:56.140 --> 00:11:57.690
Brothers?

00:11:57.690 --> 00:11:59.160
Did you forget them?

00:11:59.160 --> 00:12:02.460
They're your half-brothers.

00:12:02.820 --> 00:12:06.200
<i>Brother Walter and Brother Karl?</i>

00:12:06.200 --> 00:12:08.790
Which means... We're poor nobles, and I'm...

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:13.150
The 8th son? Are you kidding me?!

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:13.960
"The 8th Son? Are You Kidding Me?"

