00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.890
The Kingdom of Helmut

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:47.350
So this is the kingdom I live in.

00:13:47.890 --> 00:13:56.440
Capital
\h\h\h\h\h\hStuttburg

00:13:48.170 --> 00:13:51.890
Uh, this is the capital, Stuttburg,

00:13:51.890 --> 00:13:55.210
and its population is one million, 
the highest in the kingdom.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:14:01.150
South of it is the Dukedom of Bleichröder,

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:13.040
Dukedom of
\h\h\h\h Bleichröder

00:13:56.190 --> 00:14:13.040
Breichburg

00:13:56.810 --> 00:14:11.660
Minor Lords
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h Mixed Domain

00:14:01.150 --> 00:14:06.210
where the biggest mercantile center 
in the south, Breichburg, is.

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.440
Its population is two hundred thousand.

00:14:09.010 --> 00:14:13.750
And when you go even farther south

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:20.130
Rigdie Mountain Range

00:14:13.750 --> 00:14:16.860
and cross this huge mountain range,

00:14:17.280 --> 00:14:21.260
you find the back country I am 
in now, the Baumeister Knightdom.

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:31.380
Population... eight hundred.

00:14:34.020 --> 00:14:38.130
I'm the eighth son of a poor noble
 family that lives out in the sticks.

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:43.160
My life...

00:14:45.850 --> 00:14:47.300
is so screwed!

00:14:47.840 --> 00:14:49.340
We'll be going, then.

00:14:52.850 --> 00:14:55.650
Please take care of yourself.

00:14:56.160 --> 00:14:58.850
I will. You take care too, Mother.

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:02.160
Hey, where are you all going?

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:04.420
Huh? Didn't we tell you?

00:15:04.870 --> 00:15:09.630
We agreed to leave once 
Brother Kurt got married.

00:15:10.580 --> 00:15:13.690
You can stay since you're just a kid,

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:16.090
but we've long since reached adulthood.

00:15:16.090 --> 00:15:19.410
But you could inherit the lands here!

00:15:19.410 --> 00:15:23.870
You think poor nobles like us could 
afford to divide up our land?

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:26.780
It's all going to Brother Kurt.

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:31.730
We're giving up our succession rights for 
a monetary settlement and leaving home.

00:15:31.730 --> 00:15:34.560
That very moment, we cease to be nobles.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.700
Cease to be nobles?

00:15:37.700 --> 00:15:40.290
Then how are we supposed to live?

00:15:40.290 --> 00:15:43.200
Well, Brother Hermann is the second son,

00:15:43.200 --> 00:15:48.590
so he married into the branch family,
 in case anything happened to Brother Kurt.

00:15:48.590 --> 00:15:52.190
But we'll have to find our own 
path in life at the capital.

00:15:52.840 --> 00:15:57.080
We can learn to read and write, and take 
exams to be soldiers or lower management,

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.030
or look to be adventurers.

00:15:59.030 --> 00:16:02.270
It all comes down to our skills.

00:16:05.580 --> 00:16:09.740
If you keep goofing off, 
you'll regret it later, okay?

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:17.040
Goodbye.

00:16:16.160 --> 00:16:17.630
Bye!

00:16:18.080 --> 00:16:19.730
Take care!

00:16:33.800 --> 00:16:35.390
Poems of Love
Volume Eight

00:16:36.230 --> 00:16:39.800
<i>Volume Eight of Count 
Salmon's </i>Poems of Love?

00:16:39.800 --> 00:16:42.440
<i>Don't we have any useful books?</i>

00:16:52.240 --> 00:16:58.200
Magical Aptitude Crystal Ball Instruction Manual

00:16:52.390 --> 00:16:57.210
"This crystal ball can measure 
your aptitude for magic."

00:16:58.630 --> 00:17:01.120
Magic? You can't be serious.

00:17:06.160 --> 00:17:09.620
"Everyone possesses mana,

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:15.070
but it's said that only one in thousands 
has enough mana to cast magic spells.

00:17:15.070 --> 00:17:17.690
Such people are extremely rare."

00:17:18.290 --> 00:17:22.250
I knew it. I can see the "you can't 
use magic" punchline already.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:34.180
"Magical aptitude isn't hereditary.

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:41.000
Everyone has an equal chance of possessing 
the talent to be a great magician.

00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.460
Please see for yourself if you do."

00:17:44.460 --> 00:17:47.450
Who would believe this nonsense?

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.260
"If you have a talent for magic,

00:17:55.260 --> 00:17:59.710
you'll be able to shine in many fields."

00:18:04.170 --> 00:18:06.230
Hey, worth a try.

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.510
Not like I'd fall for this crap, anyway.

00:18:27.510 --> 00:18:28.870
Off we...

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:46.440
"If the crystal ball shines like a rainbow, 
you have a high aptitude for magic,

00:18:46.440 --> 00:18:52.660
in which case we recommend learning 
magic through specialized guides.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.280
Fin

00:18:54.440 --> 00:18:55.390
Fin."

00:18:57.150 --> 00:18:58.000
Huh?

00:18:58.730 --> 00:19:00.090
That's it?!

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:01.500
I need a guidebook!

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.450
Magic, magic!

00:19:03.450 --> 00:19:06.400
Magic, magic, magic...

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:09.540
Baron Montbell's
 Debauchery
 Chronicles

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:09.180
"<i>Baron Montbell's Debauchery Chronicles</i>."

00:19:09.420 --> 00:19:14.040
Count Larwen's Relaxed
 Tourism Guide

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:13.410
"<i>Count Larwen's Relaxed Tourism Guide</i>."

00:19:13.960 --> 00:19:18.380
Volume twenty-three of 
Count Salmon's <i>Poems of Love</i>.

00:19:14.040 --> 00:19:18.380
Poems of Love
Volume Twenty Three

00:19:18.870 --> 00:19:20.050
There's nothing.

00:19:21.460 --> 00:19:23.850
Oh, there you are, Wendelin.

00:19:23.850 --> 00:19:26.800
Father, do we have any other books?

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:29.780
Nope. I can't read.

00:19:31.030 --> 00:19:34.200
Anyway, could you go to the 
forest and pick up firewood?

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:45.830
Come forth, fire!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:48.280
Roar, lightning!

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:51.750
Healing Clinic!

00:19:52.660 --> 00:19:55.840
I have no idea how to activate magic.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:59.180
That was you earlier, wasn't it?

00:20:01.860 --> 00:20:05.170
I've finally found a person 
on the same wavelength as myself.

00:20:08.380 --> 00:20:11.490
Say, what is your name? Tell me.

00:20:14.410 --> 00:20:17.050
I'm sorry. I scared you, didn't I?

00:20:20.360 --> 00:20:22.020
There's no need to be afraid of me.

00:20:25.820 --> 00:20:28.000
I am a magician.

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:30.570
A magician...

00:20:51.290 --> 00:20:52.640
It spotted us!

00:21:13.970 --> 00:21:15.840
You must picture it...

00:21:17.270 --> 00:21:18.630
Your own wind magic.

00:21:18.630 --> 00:21:22.080
Magic?! Hey, don't just spring that on me!

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:26.520
First, accept the mana within you.

00:21:28.650 --> 00:21:32.840
And then, make it circulate 
through your body.

00:21:31.610 --> 00:21:33.230
What are you talking about?!

00:21:44.120 --> 00:21:45.930
D-Did I just...

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:49.130
Congratulations. You just 
used your first magic spell.

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:09.200
I am a former court magician 
of the Dukedom of Bleichröder,

00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:11.050
Alfred Rainford.

00:22:11.730 --> 00:22:13.260
Rest assured...

00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:15.980
You will become a magician 
far greater than I.
